#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bonsai2-spawn — submit one subagent task (S3.2/S3.3; MAP 3.3).

Thin deploy file; the submission flow lives in `bonsai2_harness.py`
(`cmd_spawn`) so the queue/claim protocol is shared with everything
that promotes queued tasks.

Usage (the S3.2 surface, every flag specced):
  bonsai2-spawn [-p PROMPT_FILE | -i INLINE_PROMPT]
                [--tools on|off] [--ctx N] [--deadline SECS]
                [--out FILE] [--priority low|normal|high]

Routing (S3.3, locked): the least-loaded healthy instance with a free
slot (tie-break lowest i); `bunloaded` never appears in the health
document so it is skipped by construction. No free slot on any
routable instance -> the task queues (FIFO, priority preempts: high
jumps the queue, low waits) and the spawn waits up to
`queue_wait_max_s` (harness.yaml); expiry -> exit 8, state "queued".

Exit codes (S3.2 closed set, per-command mapping):
  0  = accepted — the task is RUNNING on its instance (a free slot was
       available, or the queue wait was won within queue_wait_max_s)
  2  = malformed args / malformed config
  3  = the routing candidate is bfailed (ERR_PORT_IN_USE, S1.5) or
       bdown (ERR_INSTANCE_UNHEALTHY) at submission — S4.5: wait one
       health cycle (30 s), re-spawn
  5  = no instance's live ctx fits the requested --ctx
       (ERR_CTX_TOO_LONG, S1.5)
  8  = queue_wait_max_s expired, the task is still "queued"
  80 = main-only mode (0 instances) — the S2.4 {"reason": ...} JSON
  82 = the main endpoint is unhealthy (S3.6 probe)
  84 = health.json absent/invalid (manager down)

The task's later terminal state (done/failed/timeout, exit 20/21/22
via collect — MAP 3.6) is NOT this command's: spawn is accepted, the
worker (this dir's bonsai2-taskworker.py, started detached) owns the
run. A task id is `t-YYYYmmdd-NNNN-<4hex>` (the S3.1 example shape).
"""

import os
import sys

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
import bonsai2_harness as H  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(H.dispatch("bonsai2-spawn", sys.argv[1:]))
